# Logging (Node.js)

## Structured Logs

- **Format:** JSON; include timestamp, level, message, and context (requestId, userId, etc.)
- **Levels:** error, warn, info, debug; set level via env (LOG_LEVEL); do not log secrets or PII at info
- **Libraries:** Pino (fast), Winston (flexible)

## Correlation ID

- Generate or extract from request (header X-Correlation-ID); attach to logger (child logger or context); include in every log line for the request; propagate to downstream HTTP calls

## HTTP Logging

- Log request (method, path, correlationId); log response (status, duration); use middleware; exclude sensitive headers/body
- Log at end of request with duration; log errors with stack in development only

## Conventions

- One correlation ID per request; structured fields; no secrets; appropriate level (debug in dev, info in prod for key events)
- Use child loggers with bound context (requestId, userId) for request-scoped logs

## Anti-Patterns

- Logging full request/response with secrets; no correlation ID; unstructured strings; wrong level (error for expected 4xx)

**See also:** `error-handling.mdc`, `controllers.mdc`
